        "day": "Day 1: Arrival & Ancient Rome Views",
        "icon": "../assets/r_000646_01_4_geo-alt.svg",
        "morningActivity": "Arrive in Rome, transfer to your accommodation, and check in. Settle in and get oriented.",
        "afternoonActivity": "Gentle introduction to Rome. Walk around Piazza Venezia and view the impressive Vittoriano monument from outside. Climb to Capitoline Hill for panoramic, free views of the Roman Forum.",
        "food": "Enjoy a casual Roman dinner near your accommodation. Try Supplì (fried rice balls) as a fun, kid-friendly appetizer."
      },
      {
        "day": "Day 2: Gladiators & Emperors",
        "image": "../assets/r_000646_01_1_Colosseum_in_Rome__Italy_-_April_2007.jpg",
        "icon": "../assets/r_000646_01_2_building.svg",
        "morningActivity": "Explore the iconic Colosseum and the ancient Roman Forum. Consider a family-friendly guided tour to bring the history to life for the children.",
        "afternoonActivity": "Wander through the Palatine Hill, imagining where emperors once lived, and enjoy views over the Forum and Circus Maximus.",
        "food": "Authentic Roman pizza for lunch. Dinner at a family-friendly trattoria in the Monti neighborhood."
      },
      {
        "day": "Day 3: Vatican Wonders",
        "icon": "../assets/r_000645_01_7_house.svg",
        "morningActivity": "Visit St. Peter's Basilica & Square in Vatican City. Marvel at the scale of the basilica (remember to dress modestly: shoulders and knees covered). Look for the Swiss Guards.",
        "afternoonActivity": "Explore the Vatican Museums & Sistine Chapel. Opt for a \"skip-the-line\" ticket and focus on key highlights to keep the children engaged.",
        "food": "Indulge in"
      }
    ]
  },
